ame, doc; a NULL name ends the"] [550 2 "// fields, PyStructSequence_UnnamedField an unnamed one)"] [566 22 "// PyStructSequence_UnnamedField's value (a const char * const of the C API's data)"] [605 2 "// PyErr_SetHandledException and PyErr_SetExcInfo (Python/errors.c): the exception being handled at this level"] [606 2 "// replaced (None or NULL clears it; SetExcInfo steals its three references and keeps the value alone)"] [631 1 "// asCComplex is PyComplex_AsCComplex's value: a complex's own, else __complex__'s (a complex; a strict subclass's"] [632 1 "// instance warned of, DeprecationWarning; anything else a TypeError), else the float of o as its real part."] [666 1 "// setErrno is the world's errno set to e (EDOM 33, ERANGE 34)."] [680 1 "// cProd is _Py_c_prod with C11 Annex G.5.1's recovery of infinities computed as nan+nanj."] [718 1 "// cQuot is _Py_c_quot (Smith's algorithm by cases; a zero divisor EDOM and 0; C11 Annex G.5.2's recovery)."] [759 1 "// cPow is _Py_c_pow: b == 0 gives 1, a == 0 gives 0 (EDOM for b not real or b < 0), else the polar form, an infinite"] [760 1 "// part ERANGE (_Py_ADJUST_ERANGE2)."] [790 1 "// cAbs is _Py_c_abs: an infinite part's magnitude (even with a NaN), a NaN part NaN, else hypot, ERANGE on overflow."] [813 1 "// toDigits is b >= 0's 30-bit digits, least significant first (one digit for 0)."] [827 1 "// fromDigits is the value of 30-bit digits, least significant first."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[29 21] [29 29] [40 24] [61 31] [109 25] [126 45] [127 27] [129 32] [133 35] [169 29] [170 55] [178 25] [179 45] [180 46] [185 42] [303 20] [303 30] [421 23] [421 48] [428 15] [428 25] [429 17] [435 22] [435 30] [436 17] [454 25] [536 38] [556 43] [561 28] [567 51] [573 28] [573 30] [592 13] [592 31] [608 29] [635 41] [652 242] [668 21] [674 21] [830 22] [830 30]]} (go/file "capi_tail.go" :imports [

